      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that the line is parameterized by a parameter \\( t \\), and the vectors at \\( t = 2 \\) and \\( t = 3 \\) are given as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(t) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} \\quad \\text{when} \\quad t = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(t) = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix} \\quad \\text{when} \\quad t = 3\n\\]\n\nThe task is to find the vector on the line at \\( t = -7 \\), i.e., \\(\\mathbf{v}(-7)\\).\n\nFirst, we need to understand the relationship between the two known points on the line, \\(\\mathbf{v}(2)\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}(3)\\), using the parameter \\( t \\).\n\nLet's denote the points on the line by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(t) = \\begin{pmatrix} x(t) \\\\ y(t) \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(2) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{v}(3) = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe slope (change in vertical position over horizontal position) between these points (i.e., \\(\\frac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x}\\)) is:\n\\[\n\\frac{y_3 - y_2}{x_3 - x_2} = \\frac{\\text{change in } y}{ \\text{change in } x } = \\frac{(-4) - 4}{3 - 2} = -8\n\\]\n\n(Using \\((3, -4) - (2, 4)\\))\n \\[\n \\frac{-4 - 4}{3 - 2}\n\\vphantom{(a\\_b \\cdots_n)\n        }\n= \\frac{-8}{1}\n= -8\n\\]\n\nThis slope of \\(-8\\) will remain constant across the entire line as \\( t \\) varies. We can use this slope to express the vector \\(\\mathbf{v}(t)\\) as a linear function of \\( t \\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(t) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + (t-2) \\cdot (-8)\n\\]\n\nUsing this slope-slope form for a linear equation, we can substitute \\( t = -7 \\):\n\\[\nt - 2 = -7 - 2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(-7) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + (-9) \\cdot (-8)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(-7) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + 72\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(-7) = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + 72 \\\\ 4 + 72 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v}(-7) = \\begin{pmatrix} 73 \\\\ 76 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThus, the resulting vector on the line at \\( t = -7 \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 73 \\\\ 76 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]",
